lback branch.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': 'null'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema(null, config). The method should not throw NPE; it should delegate to loadMetaSchema.', 'description': 'Edge case where the id argument is null. The detection step should return Optional.empty, causing the fallback to be taken. Verifies robust handling of null ids.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '""'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema("", config).', 'description': 'Empty string id, also not a known dialect, should trigger the fallback branch.'}]}, {'group': 'Config parameter variations', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'A JsonMetaSchema instance equal to JsonSchemaVersion.DRAFT_07.getInstance(). The method must handle a null SchemaValidatorsConfig without throwing, and must not invoke loadMetaSchema.', 'description': 'Null config with a well‑known dialect should still resolve the dialect via SpecVersionDetector and return the corresponding meta‑schema, proving that the config argument is optional for the true branch.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"urn:custom:my-meta-schema"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema("urn:custom:my-meta-schema", null). The fallback branch must be taken and the null config must be forwarded to loadMetaSchema.', 'description': 'Null config with an unknown id forces the fallback; verifies that the method forwards a null config unchanged to loadMetaSchema and does not throw NPE.'}]}, {'group': 'Id string variations (whitespace & case)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"  http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#  "'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema("  http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#  ", config). Because the id contains surrounding whitespace, SpecVersionDetector does not recognise it, so the fallback branch is executed.', 'description': 'Tests that the detection logic is strict about whitespace; the method should treat the id as unknown and delegate to loadMetaSchema.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"HTTP://JSON-SCHEMA.ORG/DRAFT-07/SCHEMA#"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema("HTTP://JSON-SCHEMA.ORG/DRAFT-07/SCHEMA#", config). Upper‑case scheme/host makes the id unrecognised, causing fallback.', 'description': 'Ensures that id matching is case‑sensitive; a well‑known dialect written in upper case should not be detected and must trigger the custom‑schema path.'}]}, {'group': 'Malformed or non‑URI ids', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"not a uri"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema("not a uri", config). SpecVersionDetector cannot parse the string, so Optional.empty leads to fallback.', 'description': 'Validates that arbitrary non‑URI strings are safely handed over to loadMetaSchema without causing an exception.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://[invalid-ip]/schema#"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema returned by loadMetaSchema("http://[invalid-ip]/schema#", config). Even though the URI is syntactically invalid, the method should not attempt to resolve it as a known dialect and must fall back.', 'description': 'Checks robustness when the id is a malformed URI; the method should treat it as unknown and delegate to loadMetaSchema.'}]}, {'group': 'Repeated calls with same unknown id (caching behavior)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"urn:custom:cached-schema"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'First call: loadMetaSchema is invoked and its result cached. Second call: loadMetaSchema is NOT invoked again; the cached JsonMetaSchema is returned.', 'description': 'Ensures that for an unknown id the factory caches the loaded meta‑schema, preventing duplicate loading on subsequent calls.'}]}]
